{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the firstborn of a donkey you shall redeem.</b> The Sages [asked]: why was it singled out?" "<b>And they shall not appear before Me empty.</b> The males who appear — they and their children who are Mine — shall not appear without a gift in My sanctuary, but shall bring offerings." "<b>And they shall not appear before Me empty.</b> Rashi explained: according to the midrash of the baraita it is a superfluous verse and is available for a gezeirah shavah, and so he explained from ריקם ריקם, for regarding the slave it is written לא תשלחנו ריקם."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:51.091106548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}